I know nothing of this knight.  Another fool like Gawaine and you, no doubt.	我對這位騎士一無所知。想必又是個像高文和你這樣的傻子。
It will not answer.  It is sent by the Black Knight to taunt you, nothing more.	牠不會回應。牠是黑武士派來嘲弄你的，僅此而已。
You must answer the crow, Arthur.	你必須回應那隻烏鴉，亞瑟。
Of all the stubborn fools there be, I never saw such a fool as thee, You shall keep yon knight good company, And nourish the roots of Old Father Tree.	天下冥頑之徒何其多，卻不曾見過你這般執迷不悟；你將與那騎士結伴長眠，去滋養老父樹深埋的根。
There is no escape, unless I allow you to pass.  But the price of safe passage is high indeed.	此地無法脫逃，除非我允你通行。但安然通行的代價著實高昂。
Waste no time with empty words of politeness.	莫要浪費時間在虛情假意的客套話上。
That is not within your power.	那不在你的能力範圍之內。
You cannot joust with a sword.  If you accept the joust, he must perforce provide you with a jousting lance.	你不能用劍進行馬上比武。若你接受比武，他勢必得為你備妥一支比武用的長槍。
By this, I assume you mean a jousting lance.	如此看來，我猜你指的是一支比武用的長槍。
Were I with you in person, I could overcome this spell, but this is your mission and you alone must make the choices and seek the path to the Grail.	若我能親自隨你在此，或許能破除這道咒法，但這是你的使命，唯有你能自行抉擇、尋得通往聖杯的道路。
I have no use for money.	我用不著錢財。
I have no use for it.	我用不著這個。
For that insult, I shall take special pleasure in slaying you.	為了這番侮辱，我將格外樂於取你性命。
I will give you my ultimatum soon enough.	我很快便會向你下最後通牒。
Not even I know where the Grail is hidden.	就連我也不知聖杯藏於何處。
He is my prisoner.	他是我的階下囚。
I know nothing about this knight.	我對這位騎士一無所知。
My crow warned you.  You should have heeded the warning.	我的烏鴉早已警告過你，你本該聽從那警告的。
I am the Black Knight, fool.	我便是黑武士，蠢貨。
I have no equal in jousting.  You shall surely die.	馬上比武無人能與我匹敵，你必死無疑。
The black knight does not respond.	黑武士並未回應。
You disgust me.	你令我作嘔。
Praise all the powers that be! You are victorious, my king.	讚頌一切神明的力量！吾王，你得勝了。
This is no natural foe.  Nothing can be seen inside his dark, bat-winged helm and his voice is like an echo from the grave.	這絕非凡俗之敵。他那頂飾有蝙蝠翼的黑色頭盔內漆黑一片，什麼也看不見，聲音則彷彿來自墳塋深處的回響。
The Black Knight has caused a hedge to grow into a natural jousting lane divider.	黑武士使一道樹籬生長成天然的比武賽道分隔。
The Black Knight is gone.	黑武士已然離去。
Hurry on, Arthur! Gawaine must be close by!	快走，亞瑟！高文必定就在附近！
What advice can I give a fool?	我能給一個蠢貨什麼忠告？
You must joust the Black Knight if you would save Gawaine.	你若想救高文，就必須與黑武士一決比武。
Your foe awaits you at the other end of this jousting hedge.	你的對手正在這道比武樹籬的另一端等著你。
The Black Knight's body has vanished, as is to be expected with such a supernatural being.	黑武士的軀體已然消失，這等超凡之物，如此結局本在意料之中。
Only the jousting hedge remains as proof that the Black Knight was ever here.	唯有那道比武樹籬留下，證明黑武士確曾在此。
You have seen the last of him.	你已見過他最後一面。
He bears no special device.	他身上並無特殊的紋章。
I see nothing here but forest and hedge.	我在此處除了森林與樹籬，什麼也沒看見。
His helmet is adorned with two bat-like wings.	他的頭盔飾有兩片狀似蝙蝠翼的裝飾。
There is nothing to be seen there.	那裡什麼也看不見。
The jousting lane on the other side is exactly the same.  The Black Knight has not taken any unfair advantage.	另一側的比武賽道與此處完全相同，黑武士並未佔任何不公的便宜。
It is the same as this side.	與這一側相同。
It takes two to joust.	比武需要兩人方能成局。
You will pass unmolested, thanks to your cowardice. I do not know how you can bear the shame of it.	憑著你的懦弱，你將得以安然通過。我實在不明白，你如何承受得起這份恥辱。
The Black Knight is vanquished.  There is no need to escape.	黑武士已被擊敗，無須再逃。
The Black Knight is gone and left nothing behind.	黑武士已經離去，未留下任何東西。
You will not find one here.	此處找不到那樣東西。
That you can only do if you defeat the Black Knight.	唯有擊敗黑武士，你才能這麼做。
You have a chance now to save Gawaine.  Do not delay!	你現在有機會救出高文，切莫遲疑！
You have done all you could.  His fate is no longer in your hands, but that of Camelot is.  Seek the Grail.	你已盡了全力，他的命運已不再操於你手，但肯萊特的命運仍是。去尋找聖杯吧。
You can try, King Arthur, as others have died trying.	你儘管一試，亞瑟王，正如許多人曾因此一試而喪命。
You have already won your victory.	你已然贏得了這場勝利。
Too late for a show of bravado now.  The evil deed is done.	此刻逞英雄已為時已晚，惡行已然鑄成。
Your sword is of no use here.  The Black Knight has set the terms of combat as a joust.	你的劍在此無用武之地。黑武士已定下以馬上比武決勝負的條件。
Hold, King Arthur.  Do not seek to move.  Not even Merlin can free you from my power in this place.	且慢，亞瑟王。休要妄動。在此地，就連梅林也無法將你從我的力量中解救出來。
Here are your choices.	這是你的選擇。
In the forest beyond me, I have imprisoned your friend, Sir Gawaine.  He is sorely injured and shall die soon without help.  To free him, you must joust with me.	在我身後的森林裡，囚著你的摯友，高文爵士。他傷勢慘重，若無人相助，不久便將喪命。要救他，你必須與我比武。
Three times you must unhorse me before I can die.  Three times must I unhorse you to slay you.  The first knight to strike the third blow is the victor. No matter who wins, Gawaine will go free.	你須將我三度擊落馬下，我方能一死；我也須三度將你擊落馬下，方能取你性命。誰先擊出第三擊，誰便是勝者。無論誰勝，高文都將獲釋。
But if you joust with me, you will surely die.  Therefore I give you one other choice:  I will let you pass untouched.....but I will take Gawaine's life in exchange.	但若你與我比武，你必死無疑。因此我給你另一個選擇：我可讓你安然通過……但代價是高文的性命。
I lay the challenge before you.  Will you joust with me for the life of Sir Gawaine?	我在此向你下戰帖。你可願為高文爵士的性命，與我一戰？
Will you joust with me? Answer aye or nay.	你可願與我比武？請輸入「aye」或「nay」作答。
You are a weakling and a coward.  Gawaine's life is mine and you are free to go.	你是個弱者，也是個懦夫。高文的性命歸我了，你可自行離去。
Will you joust with me? Answer aye or nay.  You have no other choices.	你可願與我比武？請輸入「aye」或「nay」作答，你別無他選。
You are held fast by the power of the Black Knight.	你被黑武士的力量牢牢禁錮住了。
You are a worthy opponent.  Take up your lance and let the joust begin!	你是個夠格的對手。持起你的長槍，比武開始！
Dead men tell no tales.	死人不會洩露秘密。
Though I....did not reach the Tor....I believe it is in the possession.....of the Mad Monk of Glastonbury.	雖然我……未能抵達那座山……我相信它落在……格列斯登伯利的瘋僧侶手中。
Alas....I have not seen or heard of him since I left Camelot.	唉……自我離開肯萊特後，便再也沒見過他，也沒聽過他的消息。
Though I....did not reach the Tor....I believe the Grail is held.....by the Mad Monk of Glastonbury.	雖然我……未能抵達那座山……我相信聖杯落在……格列斯登伯利的瘋僧侶手中。
Ah...my story is not a happy one. To be defeated....by the Black Knight....I cannot bear to speak of it yet.	啊……我的遭遇並不順遂。竟敗在……黑武士手下……我此刻還無法對此啟齒。
Please, M'lord.  You must continue on with your quest.	求求你，吾王。你必須繼續你的探尋。
Now that you have saved Gawaine, concentrate once more upon your search.	如今你已救出高文，該再度專心於你的尋索之上了。
Gawaine is close to death and urgently needs help.	高文命在旦夕，亟需援手。
You let Gawaine die. I have nothing to give you at this moment but contempt.	你任由高文死去。此刻我除了鄙夷，再也給不了你別的。
This place should look familiar. It was here that you freed Gawaine and sent him back to Camelot.	這地方你應當眼熟。正是在此處，你救出了高文，並送他回肯萊特。
Gawaine's injuries are serious. Only the physicians of Camelot may be able to save him.	高文傷勢嚴重，唯有肯萊特的醫師或許還能救他。
In spite of his injuries, Gawaine has been left shackled to a massive tree.  The Black Knight shows little mercy.	高文雖已負傷，卻仍被鎖鏈拴在一株巨樹之上，黑武士毫不留情。
Naught but the proof of your shame awaits you here.  The massive tree before you marks the place where Gawaine's bones shall lie.	此處只餘你恥辱的證明。眼前這株巨樹，便是高文屍骨將要長眠之地。
He is not here.	他不在這裡。
The Black Knight still rules supreme in this forest, thanks to your cowardice.	拜你的懦弱所賜，黑武士依舊在這片森林裡稱王稱霸。
You have vanquished him, to your great glory.	你已擊敗了他，這是你莫大的榮耀。
The shackles are made of metal, sunk too deeply into the tree to pull them free, but the metal itself is not thick.	這鎖鏈是金屬打造的，深深嵌入樹身，難以硬拔脫離，但金屬本身並不厚實。
The remains of the shackles shall serve as a reminder of suffering ended.	這殘留的鎖鏈，將成為苦難已然終結的提醒。
He is safe.  Worry not.	他安然無恙，不必擔心。
I am so filled with contempt that you allowed your great friend and noble knight to die, that I can offer you no words of wisdom or comfort.	你竟任由摯友、那位高貴的騎士死去，我心中滿是鄙夷，再也給不出任何忠告或慰藉之言。
The most important thing to do is see that Gawaine reaches Camelot as quickly as possible.  But you must continue to search for the Grail.	眼下最要緊的，是設法讓高文儘快抵達肯萊特。但你仍須繼續尋找聖杯。
Gawaine is gone.	高文已經不在了。
Gawaine is still alive, barely.  Hanging from the shackles must pain him cruelly.	高文尚存一息，僅此而已。懸吊在這鎖鏈上，想必令他痛苦不堪。
Gawaine is very ill and weak.  He must go back to Camelot and be tended by a healer at once, or he will die here, but he will never make it back on foot.	高文病重體弱，必須立刻回肯萊特由醫者診治，否則便會死在此地；但他絕無可能徒步走回去。
The Black Knight has taken his life. Aye, well you should tremble at the sight. This crime lies heavily upon your own soul and will never be cleansed, no matter how you seek to right it.	黑武士已取走他的性命。是的，你見此情景理當心驚。這樁罪責將沉沉壓在你自己的靈魂之上，無論你如何試圖彌補，都永難洗清。
Alas, Gawaine, the noble Gawaine is dead.   Perhaps he died of his injuries, but I fear it was your indifference that struck the final blow.	唉，高文，高貴的高文死了。或許他是傷重不治，但我擔心，真正給予最後一擊的，是你的漠然。
He has returned to Camelot for healing.	他已回到肯萊特接受療傷。
Though he is cut and bleeding, I fear his most serious injuries may not be as obvious to the eye.	雖然他身上有傷口在流血，但我擔心他最嚴重的傷勢，未必是肉眼能看得出來的。
Does it matter how he died, be it of injuries or grief that his own king betrayed him?  He is dead.	他究竟是死於傷勢，還是死於得知自己的王背叛了他的哀痛，這重要嗎？他已經死了。
It is a huge tree.	這是一株巨樹。
Your horse has disappeared. It must have went back to Camelot.	你的坐騎已經消失了，想必是自行回了肯萊特。
I cannot believe such filth... from the lips of my own king!	我不敢相信……這等污穢之言，竟出自我王之口！
The smell of blood, sweat and illness is nearly overwhelming.	血腥、汗臭與病氣的味道幾乎令人難以承受。
I fear... I am not... my usual fragrant self.	恐怕……我此刻……並非平日那般芬芳。
The odor of human death is not a pleasant one.	人之將死所散發的氣味，並不好聞。
I am disturbed by the labored quality of Gawaine's breathing.  He must reach Camelot as quickly as possible.	高文那沉重艱難的呼吸令我不安，他必須儘快抵達肯萊特。
The pall of solemn death enshrouds this place.	一股肅穆的死亡氣息籠罩著此地。
Sir Gawaine needs more than trivialities.	高文爵士所需要的，遠不止這些瑣碎之物。
He is nearby.	他就在附近。
You are the only one who can help him.  If he does not reach Camelot quickly, he will die.	唯有你能幫助他。他若不能盡快抵達肯萊特，便將喪命。
It is too late for that.  Gawaine is dead.	那已為時已晚，高文已經死了。
Concern yourself with such things after you have freed Gawaine from his suffering.	待你解救高文脫離苦難之後，再去掛心這些事吧。
All the money in the world will not restore Sir Gawaine to life.	縱有天下所有的財富，也無法使高文爵士死而復生。
Nay, m'lord.  I will not take....your money....for you may yet need it.	不，吾王。我不會收下……你的錢……你日後或許還用得著。
Gawaine needs no gift so greatly as he needs the gift of healing, which you cannot give him, I fear.	高文最需要的，莫過於痊癒這份禮物，恐怕那並非你所能給予的。
It is of no use to a dead man.	這東西對死者毫無用處。
It can do nothing for Gawaine.	這對高文於事無補。
What morbid thoughts.	好陰鬱的念頭。
It cannot wash the stain of Gawaine's death from your soul.  He will be enfolded into the body of mother earth and this ancient tree shall be his monument.	這洗不去高文之死在你靈魂上留下的污點。他將回歸大地之母的懷抱，這株古樹便是他的紀念碑。
For what you have allowed to happen, there can be no forgiveness.	對於你所縱容發生的事，沒有寬恕可言。
You have no need of forgiveness. Your virtue, at the moment, is intact.	你不需要寬恕。此刻，你的德行仍完好無損。
You do not have your mule.	你的騾子不在你身邊。
Nothing can help him until he is free of the shackles.	除非先解開鎖鏈，否則什麼都幫不了他。
Only the healers of Camelot can save him, if he can reach them in time.  He will never make it back on foot.	唯有肯萊特的醫者能救他，前提是他能及時抵達。他絕無可能徒步走回去。
Have no fear. Gawaine will be tended well in Camelot.	不必擔憂，高文在肯萊特會受到妥善照料。
My, your memory is short. You have already shattered the shackles.	哎呀，你的記性可真差，你早已打碎那鎖鏈了。
Nothing you do now can restore Sir Gawaine to life.	你此刻做什麼，都無法讓高文爵士死而復生。
You have dealt with the shackles.	你已經處理過那副鎖鏈了。
These shackles do not unlock.	這副鎖鏈並無鎖孔可開。
I am sure you will find a way.	我相信你會想出辦法的。
The shackles are securely anchored.  Can you think of nothing better to try.	這副鎖鏈固定得十分牢靠，你就想不出更好的辦法嗎？
Not all the sword brandishing in the world will return Gawaine to life. Be still.	縱使揮盡天下劍術，也無法使高文死而復生，且靜下心來吧。
There is no danger for the moment. Best to put up your sword lest it make Gawaine uneasy.	此刻並無危險，還是收起你的劍為好，免得讓高文心生不安。
There is no danger for the moment. Or did you have some other purpose in drawing your sword?	此刻並無危險。還是說，你拔劍另有別的用意？
This is one place where it would be best to use your sword on foot.	這是個最好徒步持劍應戰的地方。
There is no danger here. Be more specific about what non-violent use you portend.	此處並無危險。請說明白些，你打算做何種非暴力的用途。
Help me, Arthur. The pain....is terrible.	救救我，亞瑟。這痛楚……難以忍受。
Beware....the Mad Monk....of Glastonbury.	小心……格列斯登伯利的……瘋僧侶。
